- Why this evidence belongs to a STARTUP region rather than to a flow capture.  The
  permission evaluator's scan runs from afterPropertiesSet(), so it is driven by the
  container's bean lifecycle and completes before any request is served.  A capture
  taken during an application flow would observe the CONSEQUENCES of that scan
  without ever observing the scan, which is why the scan is archived here and the
  permission-dependent flow assertions live in the flow captures.
- PRESERVE-list obligation, honoured explicitly.  Security and permission-evaluation
  outcomes are on the migration's PRESERVE list.  The permission evaluator and the
  reflection scanning that supports it are UNCHANGED: no signature, no scanned
  package, no scanner configuration and no library version differs between the two
  sides.  Nothing in this file implies, proposes or performs any change to the
  permission evaluator or to any permission-evaluation outcome, and this region is
  where a reviewer sees that the scan completed identically rather than being told
  that it did.
